statement:
Let n, N ∈ ℕ, M, K ⊆ ℝᴺ (ℝᴺ = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) = Rn N) and φ : ℝ → ℝᴺ → ℝᴺ. Write X := initialVelocity φ, T_y := tangentSpace M y, P_y := tangentProjection M y and B_y(τ, η) := secondFundamentalForm M y τ η.

Assume:
(a) M is a measurable set;
(b) y ↦ P_y is continuous on M;
(c) X is C¹ on ℝᴺ;
(d) K is closed;
(e) X(x) = 0 for every x ∉ K;
(f) M ∩ K is compact;
(g) μHE[n](M ∩ K) < ∞;
(h) for every y ∈ M and all τ, η ∈ T_y, ⟨η, DX(y)τ⟩ = −⟨X(y), B_y(τ, η)⟩.

Then:
(i) stableSecondVariationIntegrand M φ y = 0 for every y ∈ M with y ∉ K;
(ii) stableSecondVariationIntegrand M φ is integrable on M with respect to μHE[n].
